    <!-- file server -->
    <string name="srv_title">File server</string>
    <string name="srv_intro">Browse, download, and upload this phone\'s folders from a computer\'s browser or an FTP client. It\'s off by default, runs only while the switch below is on, and shows a notification.</string>
    <string name="srv_folder">Shared folder</string>
    <string name="srv_allow_upload">Allow uploads (new files and folders)</string>
    <string name="srv_http">HTTP server (browser)</string>
    <string name="srv_ftp">FTP server</string>
    <string name="srv_footer">Access requires a random token generated each time the server starts, and repeated wrong attempts are temporarily blocked. Existing files can\'t be overwritten, deleted, or renamed. Protected folders and vaults are never shared. Both servers use unencrypted plain-text communication.</string>
    <string name="srv_warn_title">Visible on your network</string>
    <string name="srv_warn_http">When the server is on, anyone on the same Wi-Fi (or Tailscale network) as this phone can try to connect to its address. Only people with the token can get in, but traffic isn\'t encrypted, so others on the same network can see it. Don\'t turn it on at cafés or on public Wi-Fi; use it only at home or over Tailscale. Turn it off when you\'re done.</string>
    <string name="srv_warn_ftp">When the server is on, anyone on the same Wi-Fi (or Tailscale network) as this phone can try to connect to its address. With FTP, the password (token) and files are sent unencrypted. Don\'t turn it on on public Wi-Fi; use it only at home or over Tailscale. Turn it off when you\'re done.</string>
